uith@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/95/367095/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Id945a9f8f2b45271c903f1ec038366da47f5d436" commit="c737b07ee2a04f1cb0cf40577520ea4607f7f6ea" commit_message="[autotest]only accept hosts when both hosts and meta_hosts given for a clone job  When cloning a job via autotest frontend, if user chooses the default clone action, which is 'Reuse any similar hosts' and then later still select specific hosts in the next tab, the host scheduler will get confused about the case and would try to schedule two same jobs to one host. In this case, the host scheduler will crash because of duplicate entries for one job in the database. The fix is to only accept the hosts variables under this situation.  BUG=chromium:611064 TEST=unittest  Change-Id: Id945a9f8f2b45271c903f1ec038366da47f5d436 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/366795 Commit-Ready: Dan Shi &lt;dshi@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Shuqian Zhao &lt;shuqianz@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Fang Deng &lt;fdeng@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dan Shi &lt;dshi@google.com&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="366795" owner_email="shuqianz@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/95/366795/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I29dee8263ec35ff1256e6388cc1accef3779dfba" commit="fc9436ae22f0437eb1635315aead62a770ef6169" commit_message="Modifying audio_MediaBasicVerification to skip non-headphone devices.  The test audio_MediaBasicVerification.py is failing on some devices because it is trying to verify headphone behavior even though these devices have no headphone jack. This is change is meant to skip the test for such devices.  BUG=None TEST=Tested on chromeos1-row2-rack3-host3, chromeos1-row5-rack7-host1  Change-Id: I29dee8263ec35ff1256e6388cc1accef3779dfba Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/366055 Commit-Ready: Dan Shi &lt;dshi@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Vinayak Suley &lt;vsuley@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Kalin Stoyanov &lt;kalin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Vinayak Suley &lt;vsuley@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="2" gerrit_number="366055" owner_email="vsuley@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/55/366055/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ib0df2698f397cab964f367cedbd3464e90ee3a94" commit="bb6bd21a62dfbc6fbcbe0f6f865dfd9d91fcdbef" commit_message="CRAS: alsa_io - Add default values for Line out node  We have codec detects both headphone and line out, but only one of headphone of line-out will be detected at any time. In this case there will be two jacks and nodes created for each. Add node default values for 'Line Out' node so Chrome UI can see both cases as the same type of audio out option.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:55239 TEST=On Kevin, plug headphone jack or speaker jack should trigger an audio output option on UI.  Change-Id: Ib0df2698f397cab964f367cedbd3464e90ee3a94 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/363663 Commit-Ready: Dan Shi &lt;dshi@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Hsinyu Chao &lt;hychao@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dylan Reid &lt;dgreid@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="363663" owner_email="hychao@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="5" project="chromiumos/third_party/adhd" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/adhd" ref="refs/changes/63/363663/5" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Id8cb4dc497af416ebf8bf31dae8519c168ff8eaf" commit="eebd6c421377747ad353643c750334d258bf8547" commit_message="login: Add flags for ash palette and quick unlock.  BUG=chromium:616112 TEST=Will verify ash palette and quick unlock is enabled on deployed image.  Change-Id: Id8cb4dc497af416ebf8bf31dae8519c168ff8eaf Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/365141 Commit-Ready: Dan Shi &lt;dshi@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Jacob Dufault &lt;jdufault@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dan Erat &lt;derat@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="3" gerrit_number="365141" owner_email="jdufault@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/41/365141/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="3"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I268abe40e744c9dace0ded9082abbf1a52913f4c" commit="a0ae0350071f84075d1c23d645219f2ee10f607c" commit_message="Support EV_MSC event types for ChromeOS  A vendor reported the remote chromeos support crashing when EV_MSC events were emitted by their touch device.  This seems to be due to evtest reporting those events as hexidecimal values instead of base-10. According to evtest's source there are only 2 events that it does this for, so this CL adds in a check for those events in an attempt to parse them correctly.  BUG=chromium:627506 TEST=manually tested, then verified by the vendor  Change-Id: I268abe40e744c9dace0ded9082abbf1a52913f4c Signed-off-by: Charlie Mooney &lt;charliemooney@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/359945 Commit-Ready: Dan Shi &lt;dshi@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Andrew de los Reyes &lt;adlr@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="5" gerrit_number="359945" owner_email="charliemooney@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/touch_firmware_test" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/touch_firmware_test" ref="refs/changes/45/359945/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="5"/><pending